---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import StoryLabel from '../components/StoryLabel.astro';
---
<Base title="Editorial standards" description="How M/KE reports: what our story labels mean, how we use sources, and how we correct mistakes.">
  <article class="page prose" style="max-width:760px">
    <h1>How we report</h1>
    <p>M/KE is independent. Readers should always know how solid a story is, so every piece carries one of four labels.</p>
    <p><StoryLabel label="Confirmed" /> Announced officially, or verified on the record by M/KE.</p>
    <p><StoryLabel label="Report" /> Our own reporting from sources, not yet official. We say how many sources and how we know them, without naming them.</p>
    <p><StoryLabel label="Opinion" /> Analysis or a take, signed by its writer. It's an argument, not a fact.</p>
    <p><StoryLabel label="Rumour" /> Circulating, but not verified by us. We use this sparingly and always say where it comes from.</p>
    <h2>Interviews</h2>
    <p>We publish answers as given. We fix typos and obvious grammar, never the meaning. If we translate a quote, the person sees the English before it goes live.</p>
    <h2>Corrections</h2>
    <p>When we get something wrong, we fix it and add a dated note at the end of the story saying what changed. We never edit silently.</p>
    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Spotted a mistake, or have a story? Email <a href="mailto:contact@mkegg.com">contact@mkegg.com</a>.</p>
  </article>
</Base>
